{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>אספר</b> — Some say: like <b>אספרם מחול ירבון</b> (Psalms 73:4), and similar to it <b>מי יספר שחקים בחכמה</b> (Job 38:37), and the meaning is that he is thin and has no flesh. But what seems right to me: because he mentioned <b>והתפרדו כל עצמותי</b> (Psalms 22:15), he said: when I count how many bones of mine will be separated, my enemies will laugh — like <b>לראוה בך</b> (they gaze at you). And it is possible that the bones are by way of allegory for his men who separated from him at the time of his distress in battle."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:15.536686448Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}